assets:[
{n:"US Stocks",s:"BEARISH",l:["S&P ~7,176 <span class=down>−2.02%</span> to 7,175.83, a sixth straight loss and the longest losing streak since April 2024; it is now ~8.2% below last month's record and all 11 sectors fell (AP, CNBC, Xinhua)", "Dow ~49,097 <span class=down>−2.19%</span> (−1,101 pts), its first close below 50,000 since June; Nasdaq ~23,879 <span class=down>−2.25%</span> after being up as much as 2% early (CNBC, Investing.com)", "AI reversal: stocks hit session lows the moment Anthropic began trading; Nvidia −3.3%, AMD −7.7% on a short-seller report, CoreWeave −6.1%; Williams-Sonoma −15%, while Palo Alto +6.4% on earnings (AP via BNN Bloomberg, Investing.com)", "Breadth was very weak: 10 NYSE new highs vs 423 new lows, and decliners beat advancers 2,339 to 515 on the NYSE (WSJ Markets Diary, Investing.com)", "VIX rose to its highest since March; after hours, a Bloomberg report that Apple is building its own AI agent weighed on Meta and Anthropic (Yahoo Finance)"]},
{n:"Bonds",s:"BEARISH",l:["10Y ~5.05%: −2bp to 5.046% as falling stocks drove a safe-haven bid (a fourth straight daily drop); the 2Y fell 4bp to ~4.76%, the 30Y ~5.40% (CNBC, Investing.com)", "Fed odds (19 Nov): a quarter-point December hike is ~95% priced (CME FedWatch via CNBC)", "Data: jobless claims 203k vs 197k expected (still low); the Philly Fed factory index sank to 6.3 from 20.9 while prices paid jumped to 58.2 (CNBC, Reuters via Investing.com, CoinDesk)", "Fed talk: Chicago Fed's Goolsbee says the Fed's job is to keep the AI investment surge from overheating the economy; Waller still wants 50bp (CoinDesk, CNBC)", "Next: Wed 25 Nov PCE inflation, durable goods and jobless claims; Fed decision 8-9 Dec (Schaeffer's, CNBC)"]},
{n:"Oil",s:"BEARISH",l:["WTI ~$83.2 <span class=down>−0.1%</span> settled $83.21 (−$0.05), still the lowest since 26 August; the December contract expires Friday (Reuters via Investing.com, Rigzone, Xinhua)", "Brent ~$92.0 <span class=up>+0.0%</span> settled $91.98 (+$0.03) after swinging between ~$91.2 and $93.5; down ~20% this month (Rigzone, Newsquawk)", "US diesel ~$5.93/gal national average (AAA, 19 Nov), easing; NYMEX ULSD −0.5% to $3.95/gal and European diesel futures hit a three-month low (AAA, DTN, Rigzone)", "Push and pull: Iran's IRGC claimed two supertankers hit mines in Hormuz (not independently verified) and Trump is weighing new strikes, but US stockpiles are rising and the Trump-Xi-Putin declaration promises more fuel supply (Reuters via Investing.com, Newsquawk, Rigzone)", "Hormuz flows hit a record, says the US energy chief; the IEA says oil and gas could become buyers' markets if the war ends soon (Rigzone)"]},
{n:"Gold",s:"BEARISH",l:["~$3,600 spot <span class=down>−3.3%</span> (Kitco $3,600.10 late Thursday NY; ~$3,606 at ~06:50 ICT Friday), a fresh 14-month low; silver −4.7% to ~$42.8 (Kitco)", "Why weak: more Fed-hike bets, a dollar near its 19-month high and another stock sell-off; even US-Iran tension brought no lasting haven bid (Kitco)", "Watch $3,590 (Thursday's low); $3,650 and $3,700 are now resistance (Kitco)"]},
{n:"Bitcoin",s:"BEARISH",l:["~$61,900 <span class=down>−2.0%</span> early Friday ($61,852 at ~06:50 ICT), after dropping to $61,800 Thursday — the lowest since early July (CoinGecko, CoinDesk)", "Why still bearish: >$300M of spot-ETF outflows Wednesday, 70% of options volume in puts, and it fell with stocks; on track for a 7th straight weekly loss (CoinDesk)", "Ether ~$1,753 (−1.5%); watch ~$62k (lost) and the July lows (CoinGecko, CoinDesk)"]}],
