DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>Don't read a hot IPO as an all-clear.</b> Anthropic closed 17% above its $83 IPO price but 13% below its $111.50 open, and the S&P fell 2% the same day. If you want AI exposure, a broad index fund already holds the big AI names.",
"<b>Keep investing regularly, not all at once.</b> Fear & Greed fell to 19 (Extreme Fear) and NYSE new lows (423) swamped new highs (10) as the S&P fell a sixth day. Fixed monthly buys (DCA) beat guessing the bottom.",
"<b>Plan for more rate hikes.</b> A December hike is ~95% priced and Fed officials keep warning about inflation and AI overheating; lock fixed rates where you can and avoid new variable-rate debt.",
"<b>Cash and short bonds still pay you to wait.</b> With the 2Y near 4.76% and hikes coming, keep your emergency fund and near-term money in high-yield savings or short-term bonds.",
"<b>Don't panic-sell a down week.</b> The S&P is ~8% below its record — a normal pullback so far. Selling after big drops locks in losses; rebalance only if your mix has drifted far from plan.",
"<b>Fuel relief continues.</b> WTI is near its lowest since August, US diesel is ~$5.93 and Thailand cut diesel B7 to ฿39.99; Iran strike talk can still cause spikes, so budget for swings.",
"<b>Gold is a hedge, not a rocket.</b> It fell another ~3% to ~$3,600, a 14-month low, as rate-hike bets and a strong dollar bite; hold a small slice for protection rather than trying to catch the bottom.",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> BTC ~$62k is at its lowest since July and heading for a 7th weekly loss; only invest what you can afford to see fall a lot more.",
"<b>Thai investors: stay selective.</b> The SET held flat at 1,472.64 but foreigners sold ฿2.5B and the baht touched 34.02; brokers see 1,460-1,490. Favour steady dividend payers over chasing.",
"<b>War headlines swing both ways.</b> A Trump-Xi-Putin peace declaration and Iran strike talk landed the same day and oil ended flat — avoid trading on headlines and keep a diversified mix."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 19 (18.7) = Extreme Fear, down from 25 Wednesday and 40 a week ago, about level with 20 a month ago. Momentum, put/call, VIX and safe-haven demand read extreme fear; price strength, breadth and junk bonds read fear."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~49.0 = Elevated (up from 48.5): Trump is weighing new Iran strikes and Iran claims tankers hit mines in Hormuz, partly offset by the Trump-Xi-Putin peace declaration."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 1.2 = extreme fear, down from 4.8 as the S&P fell further below its 200-day average."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 31.2 = fear, down from 34.0; NYSE had 423 new lows vs 10 highs."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 30.8 = fear, down from 40.2 as decliners swamped advancers."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 7.2 = extreme fear, from 10.2: traders keep buying downside protection."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. 13.3 on CNN's 0-100 scale = extreme fear, down from 29.1 as the VIX hit its highest since March."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 9.0 = extreme fear, from 12.6; bonds rallied while stocks fell 2%."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 38.6 = fear, down from 41.4 as demand for junk bonds cooled further."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 70 (from 68): Trump is weighing a new joint strike campaign with Israel; Iran claims two tankers hit mines."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 42 (from 40): Russian drones hit Kyiv during the summit and Putin vowed 'far more painful' retaliation over the Crimea bridge."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 90 (from 89): Iran resumed drone attacks on US bases in Kuwait and Bahrain and claims mined tankers in Hormuz."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 8 (from 9): Trump, Xi and Putin held three-way talks and issued a joint peace declaration."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 28 (from 32): the Shenzhen declaration says nuclear war 'must never be fought' and backs dialogue on nuclear risks, but no treaty yet."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~7,176 Thursday (−2.02%), a sixth straight loss, the longest slide since April 2024."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. −2.19% Thursday (−1,101 pts) to about 49,097, the first close under 50,000 since June."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. −2.25% Thursday to about 23,879 after being up 2% early, as AI stocks reversed during Anthropic's debut."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~5.05% Thursday, down ~2bp as investors sought safety, even with a December hike ~95% priced."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$83.2 (−0.1%) Thursday, flat near its lowest since late August; the December contract expires Friday."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. ~$92.0 at Thursday's settle (+0.03%), down ~20% this month."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$5.93/gal (AAA, 19 Nov), still easing."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$3,600 spot (−3.3%), a 14-month low, as rate-hike bets, a strong dollar and falling stocks bite."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$62k = still bearish: −2% to its lowest since July with ETF outflows; it trades with tech, not as a haven."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00% after September's hike, held 28 Oct; a December hike is ~95% priced for 8-9 Dec."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. October rose 0.4% MoM (est. 0.3%) and core 0.3% (est. 0.2%), a third straight upside surprise; no official YoY because of last year's data gap, well above the Fed's 2% goal."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. October rose 0.3% MoM (est. 0.4%) and 6.5% YoY, the highest since November 2022; core +0.3%."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). ~95% for a quarter point in December."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. ~103.9 Thursday, near Wednesday's 19-month high."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. ~159.7, just under the 160 level where Japan has warned about intervention."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) in October; its bonds now yield ~15% (CNBC, 17 Nov)."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision|BoT held|BoT kept",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. Held at 1.00% on 28 Oct; Governor Witai says the BoT aims to keep rates steady to support growth but is data-dependent; 2026 GDP forecast kept at 2.4%; next decision 23 Dec."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. 1,472.64 Thu 19 Nov (+0.04%) after dipping to 1,454; LH Securities sees 1,460-1,490."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. −฿2,495M of Thai stocks on Thu 19 Nov, after near-flat (−฿34M) Wednesday."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};

